# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# Generated site data — every build writes here (slates, fantasy, NBA,
# Polymarket, UFC) and `ledger.export_json` writes record.json, which is
# the operator's own betting journal and bankroll. All of it regenerates
# from the build scripts, none of it belongs on the remote. Ignoring the
# directory (not a file list) so a NEW build target can't silently start
# tracking output again.
web/data/

# Downloaded / cached data feeds
data/cache/

# Trained models (regenerate with: python3 train_model.py)
data/models/

# Local API keys — never commit these
# Every shape of the secrets file, not just the exact name. An editor's
# backup holds the same keys as the original: nano writes secrets.local.save
# on an interrupted edit, vim writes .swp and ~, and a hand-made copy is
# usually secrets.local.bak. One of those sat untracked-but-visible in this
# repo with two live API keys in it, one `git add -A` from a public push.
secrets.local
secrets.local.*
secrets.local~
*.local.save
# The Yahoo OAuth token. Not an API key but the same class of object and
# worse to leak: it is scoped to ONE person's fantasy account and grants
# read access until it is revoked. `data/` is not ignored as a directory
# here — only named files under it are — so this needs saying explicitly,
# which is exactly the hole `data/*.pre-rescale-*` below was added for.
data/yahoo_token.json

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Historical database (populate with: python3 ingest.py)
data/history.db
*.db
data/ledger.db
# The auto-update timer's own state (deploy/autoupdate.py). MUST stay
# ignored: the updater refuses a dirty tree, and `git status --porcelain`
# lists untracked files — unignored, the state file the updater writes
# would jam the updater itself on its second run.
data/autoupdate.json
# Rocket Radar's own record — the calls, their marks and their
# paths. Same reasoning as the bet ledger: it is the machine's
# memory of what it said, not source, and it only means anything
# on the box that made the calls.
data/memeledger.db
data/backups/
# The sim-joint evidence journal (simjoint.build appends, simrecon.py
# grades) — per-box measurement data, like the databases above it.
data/simrecon_log.jsonl
# The drive sim's forward journal (engine/drivesim.py; nfl_build
# appends) — same contract, graded by the clock-sport reconciliation.
data/drivesim_log.jsonl
# The sweat page's probability history (engine/sweat.py, written on the
# 12-second live clock). Missing from this file, it sat untracked on
# the droplet and jammed the auto-update timer for a day — 2026-08-31.
data/sweatstate.json
# The FULL boards — every pick, before redaction. These are the product,
# and they live outside web/ precisely so no web server can reach them;
# committing them would publish to GitHub what the paywall withholds from
# the site. `*.db` and the named files above do not cover a .json here.
data/built/
# The feed differ's per-sport digests — working state, rolls every cycle
data/feedstate/
# backup.sh's default destination is ./backups — a sibling of data/, not a
# child of it, so the line above never covered it. The files inside are
# `.db.gz`, which `*.db` does not match either: gzipped copies of the
# accounts and ledger databases, untracked, one `git add -A` from being
# published. On the server these live in /var/backups/qellys instead; this
# is for the laptop, where the script is run from the checkout.
backups/
# …and the backups a migration leaves BESIDE the database. `*.db` does not
# cover them: rescale.py writes `ledger.db.pre-rescale-<date>`, which ends
# in a date, so it showed up as a perfectly ordinary untracked file. One
# `git add -A` and the whole bet journal is public. Found on the real
# machine 2026-08-07 with such a file sitting untracked in data/.
data/*.pre-rescale-*
data/*.bak
data/*.backup
# …and SQLite's write-ahead log and shared-memory files. `*.db` does NOT
# match `accounts.db-wal`, and the WAL holds writes that have not been
# checkpointed yet — for the accounts database that means email addresses
# and password verifiers sitting in a file git was perfectly willing to
# track. Exactly the `.pre-rescale-` hole, found the same way: by a test
# that names the real files rather than trusting the pattern.
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal
# Runtime state written next to the databases — a spend counter and a
# failure log, both machine-local and both meaningless in anyone else's
# clone. Same reasoning as the UFC dossiers below.
data/llm_spend.json
data/sim_gate_failures.json
# Both forms on purpose. A trailing slash matches DIRECTORIES ONLY, and a
# symlink is not a directory to git — so `node_modules/` alone let a symlink
# named node_modules be committed, pointing at a scratchpad path that exists
# on no other machine. That broke `git pull` for everyone else with
# "Updating the following directories would lose untracked files".
node_modules
node_modules/

# Node is only ever used by tools/inventory.mjs, which resolves Playwright
# from a scratchpad symlink. A package.json in the repo root is a leftover of
# an npm run in the wrong directory, not a dependency of this project.
package.json
package-lock.json

# Generated UFC reference data — ufc_dossiers.py and the card/gym scrapers
# write these beside the DBs. Same rule as every other data/ artifact: the
# build regenerates them, so they never belong in the repo.
data/ufc_cards.json
data/ufc_dossiers.json
data/ufc_gyms.json

# Nightly runner: local logs and its overlap lock.
logs/
.nightly.lock
